---
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---
<Layout title="Privacy & Security: How Tether Protects Your Files" description="What Tether stores, what it never sees, and how clipboard sync and file transfers between your devices are encrypted, peer-to-peer and never uploaded.">
  <article class="wrap doc">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy &amp; security</p>
    <h1>What we see, and what we <span class="serif">never do.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Tether is built so your clips and files go straight from one browser to another. This page lists exactly what passes through our server and what doesn't.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Files</h2>
      <p>Files travel only over a direct, encrypted WebRTC connection between the browsers in your session. They are never uploaded, stored or relayed by our server. If a direct connection can't be made, Tether tells you the file can't be sent rather than routing it elsewhere.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Text clips</h2>
      <p>Clips also use the direct connection. Only when no direct link can be made (some strict corporate or mobile networks block it), a clip is passed through our server to the other person and is not stored. It exists only in memory while being forwarded.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Encryption</h2>
      <p>Every direct connection is encrypted with DTLS, the standard built into all browsers for video calls and data channels. Keys are generated in your browser for each connection. The site itself is served only over HTTPS.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What the server keeps</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>For each session:</b> a random session ID, the current 6-digit join code (valid 10 minutes), an invite token, and each person's display name and 4-character device tag.</li>
        <li><b>While you're connected:</b> the status you choose to share (for example "Working in Figma" or your Spotify track), held in memory and never written to disk.</li>
        <li><b>Rate limits:</b> a short-lived counter per IP address to stop people guessing join codes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>A session and everything in it is deleted automatically after 12 hours with nobody connected. Seats unused for 15 minutes are freed.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>On your device</h2>
      <p>Your name and device tag are kept in a cookie in your browser (up to 400 days) so you don't retype them. Your clip history is kept in this browser tab only and disappears when you close it. There are no accounts, no passwords, no email, and no advertising or analytics trackers.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Spotify (optional)</h2>
      <p>If you connect Spotify, the sign-in and the "now playing" lookups happen directly between your browser and Spotify. Only the track title and artist are shown to the people in your session.</p>
    </section>

    <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to Tether</a></p>
  </article>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .doc { max-width: 720px; padding-block: 48px 80px; }
  .doc h1 { margin: 12px 0 16px; font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 48px); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.045em; font-weight: 600; }
  .doc h1 .serif { color: var(--accent-text); font-size: 1.1em; }
  .lede { font-size: 17px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 32px; }
  section { padding-block: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  section p, li { color: var(--muted); }
  section b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  ul { padding-left: 18px; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .back { margin-top: 32px; }
</style>
